---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Why I started LightPhotos — LightPhotos Blog"
  desc="A Lightroom license stopped working after a macOS upgrade, and a newer Apple Photos did not open years of my photos. One afternoon, I gave up and built the small editor that I actually needed."
  active="blogs"
>
  <main class="lp-page">
    <article class="lp-article">
      <header class="lp-article-head">
        <p class="lp-article-meta"><a href="/blogs.html">Blogs</a> &middot; <time datetime="2026-06-23">June 23, 2026</time></p>
        <h1>Why I started LightPhotos</h1>
        <p class="lp-article-dek">
          A Lightroom license stopped working, and I could not open years of
          photos from Apple Photos. One afternoon, I gave up and built the
          small editor that I actually needed.
        </p>
        <p class="lp-article-byline">Andrew Yao &middot; 4 min read</p>
      </header>

      <aside class="lp-tldr">
        <p class="lp-tldr-label">TL;DR</p>
        <p>
          I paid for Lightroom 6, and after a macOS upgrade I could not install
          it again. A few upgrades later, a newer Apple Photos did not open the
          libraries on my old backups, and I lost years of photos. Free editors
          such as Darktable wanted me to learn a whole craft, when I only wanted
          to send some pictures to my friends. So I listed what I needed and
          built the smallest editor that does it. Coding
          agents wrote most of the code.
        </p>
      </aside>

